# Two code owners, so neither one's own pull request can pass on the automated
# review's approval alone: GitHub waives the code-owner rule when the author is
# the only owner, and the review's approval would then count.
# Review is required on everything, and specifically on the paths that decide
# what CI may do and what the automated review lets through: the workflows,
# which deploy to dev and stg and hold their credentials, and the review's
# rules.
#
# Once the dev and stg rulesets require code-owner approval, an approval from
# the automated review never counts toward a merge: only these people's does.

*                               @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/workflows/**           @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/claude-review/**       @drn1996 @frubble-platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @drn1996 @frubble-platform
